<title>JAPAN: Japan Jan tin imports up 3.6 pct year/year -- MOF.</title>
<headline>Japan Jan tin imports up 3.6 pct year/year -- MOF.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-02-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Japan imported 2,167 tonnes of refined tin in January, up 3.6 percent from 2,092 tonnes in the same month last year, Finance Ministry data said on Friday.</p>
<p>The imports (on a customs-cleared basis in tonnes) were as follows:</p>
<p>			Jan 97	   Dec 96	  Jan 96</p>
<p> Total		2,167	    2,050	    2,092</p>
<p>Major suppliers:</p>
<p> Indonesia	  1,020	    1,048		799</p>
<p> Malaysia	     661		497		599</p>
<p>Cumulative imports in 1996 were 25,272 tonnes, off 9.8 percent from 28,019 tonnes the year before.</p>
<p>-- Tokyo Commodities Desk +81-3 3432 6179</p>
</text>
